  "id": "COMPOUND:27769 - PROTEIN:5793",
  "verbalization": "Pandaroside I is implicated in the targeting of Hepatocyte through multiple indirect pathways, all of which converge on the MIP molecule. The evidence suggests that Pandaroside I acts as a target for various compounds, including S-ethylcysteine zwitterion and a complex natural product, ultimately leading to a direct interaction with Hepatocyte. This indicates a potential mechanism where Pandaroside I may influence cellular processes in hepatocytes through these intermediates. The shared pathway of targeting MIP and subsequent interaction with Hepatocyte suggests a possible role in hepatotoxicity or metabolic regulation, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, emphasizing the importance of further investigation into the functional roles of these intermediates.",
